## Health System, Services and Operational Units
- [Directorate General of Public Health](https://hsgm.saglik.gov.tr/):
  Official source for protecting and improving public health; combating health risk factors; conducting primary healthcare services and operating primary care facilities; carrying out surveillance, immunization, and control programs for communicable, non-communicable and chronic diseases, cancer, and risk groups (maternal, child, adolescent, elderly, disabled); supporting healthy lifestyle habits; combating tobacco, obesity and nutrition-related risks; organizing laboratory services for individual, community and environmental health; establishing and operating national reference laboratories; and taking measures against public health threats.
- [Directorate General of Health Services](https://shgm.saglik.gov.tr/):
  Official source for planning, regulating, and classifying all preventive, diagnostic, therapeutic, and rehabilitative health services; licensing and inspecting public and private health facilities; setting patient rights and safety standards; determining health service fee schedules; regulating specialization training, health workforce planning, registration and certification of health professionals; and developing quality and accreditation standards for health services.
- [Directorate General of Public Hospitals](https://khgm.saglik.gov.tr/):
  Official source for establishing and operating Ministry-affiliated hospitals, oral and dental health centers, and similar health facilities; ensuring delivery of all preventive, diagnostic, therapeutic, and rehabilitative health services; monitoring and evaluating service performance; conducting performance assessments; and improving patient rights and patient/staff safety in health facilities.
- [Directorate General of Emergency Health Services](https://acilafet.saglik.gov.tr/):
  Official source for planning and executing nationwide emergency and disaster health services; establishing and operating pre-hospital emergency units (112) and integrating with hospital emergency departments; managing land, air, and sea ambulances; coordinating medical rescue in domestic and international disasters; planning and procuring emergency medical supplies and radio communication infrastructure; preparedness against chemical and biological threats; and organizing public first-aid training.
- [Directorate General of Health Information Systems](https://sbsgm.saglik.gov.tr/):
  Official source for developing nationwide policy, strategy, and standards for health informatics and communication technologies; managing personal health data and health information systems at the national level; monitoring international developments in health information technology; setting rules and authorizing entities working in health informatics; and coordinating health statistics and digital health infrastructure.
- [Directorate General of Health Promotion](https://sggm.saglik.gov.tr/):
  Official source for increasing public and individual health knowledge, awareness, and control; promoting health literacy and behavior change through campaigns, educational programs, and mass media; conducting scientific studies on health promotion; reducing disease risks through healthy lifestyle programs; and managing the Ministry's public relations and information services.
- [Directorate General of Health Investments](https://sygm.saglik.gov.tr/):
  Official source for engineering and project services for Ministry and affiliated buildings; conducting construction tenders and supervision; setting health facility architectural standards; conducting expropriation procedures; executing facility construction and renewal through public-private partnership or other models; and supporting domestic and international investment in advanced medical technologies.
- [Directorate General of Management Services](https://yhgm.saglik.gov.tr/):
  Official source for Ministry personnel planning, appointment, transfer, promotion, retirement and personnel affairs; procurement, cleaning, security, maintenance, transportation, and support services; management of Ministry movable and immovable property; and general registry and archive operations.

